<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Lord, I’ve been so hardened,</l><l>Caught in worldly traffic,</l><l>Drowning out Your words that</l><l>Fell upon my wayward heart.</l><l>Somehow, still You got in,</l><l>Soft’ning up my tender parts.</l><l>How could I refuse You?</l><l>You bore me on Your wounded heart.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>I thought I was willing,</l><l>Shallowly receiving,</l><l>Meanwhile I was sinning,</l><l>Burying my shameful side.</l><l>But the sun exposed me,</l><l>Now I can no longer hide.</l><l>Bare without Your presence,</l><l>For dire help to You I fly.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Everything seemed peaceful,</l><l>Till Your words intruded,</l><l>Anxious thoughts arose and</l><l>Tried to choke the life away.</l><l>Lifelessly I drifted,</l><l>Couldn’t tell the night from day.</l><l>Then a ray of light came,</l><l>Shining through a man of clay.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
